# Qin et al. (2025), PASA 42, e049 (arXiv:2412.00799; the published Table A1 equals arXiv Table 3): volume-averaged x_HI,
#   MAP model with the [16, 84]th percentiles (both z columns of the table, 52 redshifts).
#   Posterior of a 21cmFAST-based model forward-modelling the XQR-30+ Lya forest (tau_eff distributions at z = 5.3-6.1), with
#   the UV LFs (z = 6-10) and the Planck CMB optical depth in the likelihood (fiducial model); model-based, so the z > 6 values are
#   constrained mostly through the model, not measured.
#   The MAP is the single best-fitting model and need not lie inside the 16-84% interval (7 redshifts, by 0.01).
#   Values are rounded to 0.01: 10-50% where x_HI <= 0.05. Where the MAP rounds to 0.00 (z = 4.90-5.39) the row is an upper
#   limit at the rounding bound of the 84th percentile (0.005; 0.015 at z = 5.39, where the 84th percentile is 0.01).
